.ie \n(.g .ds Aq \(aq
.el .ds Aq '
.TH rqx-comment 1  "comment " 
.SH NAME
rqx\-comment \- Post the review onto the merge request it is reviewing, and grade the commit
.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBrqx comment\fR [\fB\-\-level\fR] [\fB\-\-base\fR] [\fB\-\-dry\-run\fR] [\fB\-\-marker\fR] [\fB\-\-no\-status\fR] [\fB\-\-fail\-on\fR] [\fB\-\-allow\-findings\fR] [\fB\-\-min\-health\fR] [\fB\-\-min\-grade\fR] [\fB\-\-fail\-on\-incomplete\fR] [\fB\-\-threads\fR] [\fB\-\-config\fR] [\fB\-\-no\-tui\fR] [\fB\-\-no\-mouse\fR] [\fB\-\-color\fR] [\fB\-\-motion\fR] [\fB\-\-no\-progress\fR] [\fB\-\-progress\fR] [\fB\-v\fR|\fB\-\-verbose\fR]... [\fB\-\-hyperlinks\fR] [\fB\-h\fR|\fB\-\-help\fR] [\fIPATH\fR] 
.SH DESCRIPTION
Post the review onto the merge request it is reviewing, and grade the commit
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-\-level\fR \fI<LEVEL>\fR
relaxed, standard, strict or pristine
.TP
\fB\-\-base\fR \fI<REF>\fR
Review against this revision. Defaults to the merge request\*(Aqs own base, which the pipeline already knows
.TP
\fB\-\-dry\-run\fR
Print the comment and where it would go, and post nothing
.TP
\fB\-\-marker\fR \fI<ID>\fR [default: results]
Which comment to keep. Two jobs on one merge request each keep their own
.TP
\fB\-\-no\-status\fR
Comment, but leave the commit ungraded
.TP
\fB\-\-threads\fR \fI<N>\fR
Worker threads. Defaults to the machine\*(Aqs parallelism
.TP
\fB\-\-config\fR \fI<FILE>\fR
Read settings from this file, layered over any `rqx.yaml` found
.TP
\fB\-\-no\-tui\fR
Never open the interactive interface; bare `rqx` prints the report instead
.TP
\fB\-\-no\-mouse\fR
Leave the mouse to the terminal. The session never captures it; the flag is still accepted so an existing invocation keeps working
.TP
\fB\-\-color\fR \fI<COLOR>\fR [default: auto]
When to colour output; `auto` follows NO_COLOR and whether stdout is a terminal
.br

.br
\fIPossible values:\fR
.RS 14
.IP \(bu 2
auto
.IP \(bu 2
always
.IP \(bu 2
never
.RE
.TP
\fB\-\-motion\fR \fI<MOTION>\fR [default: on]
Animation in the interactive interface
.br

.br
\fIPossible values:\fR
.RS 14
.IP \(bu 2
on
.IP \(bu 2
off
.RE
.TP
\fB\-\-no\-progress\fR
Do not draw the progress bar on stderr; `\-\-quiet` implies it
.TP
\fB\-\-progress\fR \fI<PROGRESS>\fR [default: auto]
How a scan reports progress on stderr; `plain` prints a line every two seconds for a job log
.br

.br
\fIPossible values:\fR
.RS 14
.IP \(bu 2
auto: A bar on a terminal, nothing in CI or when stderr is redirected
.IP \(bu 2
bar: A bar whenever stderr is a terminal, CI included
.IP \(bu 2
plain: A line on stderr every two seconds and at each phase, for a job log
.IP \(bu 2
none: Nothing
.RE
.TP
\fB\-v\fR, \fB\-\-verbose\fR
Say more: \-v adds the configuration, the cache and every skipped file to the report; \-vv also prints stage timings and git commands on stderr
.TP
\fB\-\-hyperlinks\fR \fI<HYPERLINKS>\fR [default: auto]
Make file:line in the report a link that opens in your editor; `auto` only where the terminal is known to support it
.br

.br
\fIPossible values:\fR
.RS 14
.IP \(bu 2
auto: On a terminal that is known to open them
.IP \(bu 2
always: Whenever the report is coloured
.IP \(bu 2
never: Never
.RE
.TP
\fB\-h\fR, \fB\-\-help\fR
Print help (see a summary with \*(Aq\-h\*(Aq)
.TP
[\fIPATH\fR] [default: .]

.SH GATE
.TP
\fB\-\-fail\-on\fR \fI<FAIL_ON>\fR
Lowest severity that fails the run
.br

.br
\fIPossible values:\fR
.RS 14
.IP \(bu 2
info
.IP \(bu 2
warning
.IP \(bu 2
error
.IP \(bu 2
never
.RE
.TP
\fB\-\-allow\-findings\fR \fI<ALLOW_FINDINGS>\fR
Findings allowed before the run fails
.TP
\fB\-\-min\-health\fR \fI<MIN_HEALTH>\fR
Health score below which the run fails; 0 disables
.TP
\fB\-\-min\-grade\fR \fI<MIN_GRADE>\fR
Lowest grade any single file may carry
.br

.br
\fIPossible values:\fR
.RS 14
.IP \(bu 2
pristine
.IP \(bu 2
clean
.IP \(bu 2
fair
.IP \(bu 2
poor
.IP \(bu 2
critical
.IP \(bu 2
never
.RE
.TP
\fB\-\-fail\-on\-incomplete\fR
Fail when a design pattern is half applied
.SH EXTRA
Examples:
  rqx comment \-\-base main             one sticky comment, edited on every re\-run
  rqx comment \-\-dry\-run               print what would be posted, post nothing
  rqx comment \-\-marker api            a second comment for a second job

GitLab needs RQX_TOKEN or GITLAB_TOKEN with `api` scope: CI_JOB_TOKEN cannot write
merge\-request notes. GitHub needs `permissions: pull\-requests: write`, and
`statuses: write` for the commit grade.
